# Ralph loop protocol (Aegis)

When the user asks to run Ralph / overnight loop / iterate until done:

1. Read `RALPH_TASK.md`, `.ralph/progress.md`, `.ralph/guardrails.md`, `docs/PROJECT_MEMORY.md`
2. Work **one** unchecked success criterion per iteration
3. Verify with tests/commands before checking the box
4. Persist progress in `.ralph/` (not chat memory)
5. Emit `<ralph>CONTINUE</ralph>`, `<ralph>COMPLETE</ralph>`, or `<ralph>GUTTER</ralph>`
6. Obey Karpathy + engineering-discipline + `aegis-core` rules

**CLI overnight (needs cursor-agent):**

```bash
./scripts/ralph once -y
RALPH_MODEL=composer-2 ./scripts/ralph loop -n 20 -y
```

**In-IDE:** invoke `/ralph-loop` or ask for “one Ralph iteration on RALPH_TASK.md”.
